  "assumptions": [
    {
      "id": "A_SAMPLE_PLUGIN",
      "description": "Use supplied selected CHNS sample summaries as plug-in development constraints. They are estimates with sampling/selection uncertainty, not population truth. No confidence interval is used as an acceptance band, weighting precision, or p-value target. Generated draws do not encode their full uncertainty."
    },
    {
      "id": "A_AGE",
      "description": "Discrete maximum-entropy shape within age bins 35-38,39-52,53-67,68-74 with masses 0.09,0.40,0.40,0.11; fit shared linear/quadratic exponential tilt to supplied age mean/SD. The bin masses are assumptions compatible with supplied integer quantiles, not recovered empirical counts."
    },
    {
      "id": "A_MARGINS",
      "description": "BMI has one lognormal law fitted to mean/SD. Glucose and HbA1c each have a two-lognormal marginal fitted by deterministic moments/CDF equations to five supplied summaries. Positive support and finite moments follow for these finite lognormal mixtures. Distribution family and unsupplied tail behavior remain assumptions."
    },
    {
      "id": "A_DEPENDENCE",
      "description": "Four component-specific Gaussian latent vectors couple age, female, BMI and biomarker variation. Correlated mixture indicators produce additional glucose/HbA1c upper-tail association; indicators are independent of the underlying normal noise and of age/female/BMI. The broad/broad component has assumed glucose/HbA1c latent rho 0.90; the other components share a fitted lower rho. Components are statistical heterogeneity, not diagnosed diabetes or a causal mechanism. Rank and Pearson correlations are distinct fitted constraints."
    },
    {
      "id": "A_NUISANCE",
      "description": "Unknown latent correlations are age/female 0, age/BMI -0.08, female/BMI 0.04, female/glucose 0.04, female/HbA1c 0.03, BMI/glucose 0.20. These are explicit regularizing scenario choices, not inferred independence or evidence-derived signs. Female=1 means latent Z_female is below its threshold; positive latent correlations therefore imply lower continuous-variable values among females."
    },
    {
      "id": "A_OLS",
      "description": "Fit remaining three latent correlations jointly to the three supplied differently adjusted OLS projections using analytic covariances. This does not concatenate externally reported separate regressions into a structural equation, and the projections are not causal effects."
    },
    {
      "id": "A_IID",
      "description": "Generate 3000 IID selected-population rows and unique artificial identifiers. No observed participant values, community clusters, survey weights, family structure, treatments, missingness process, or diagnostic disease category are reconstructed. Evidence uncertainty is distinct from draw variation."
    },
    {
      "id": "A_MEASUREMENT",
      "description": "Generate continuous serum glucose and HbA1c values in task units without rounding or a serum/plasma conversion. Reference assay context is retained; no equivalence to external plasma measurements or external HbA1c assays is claimed."
    }
  ],
